Helicobacter</italic> spp</article-title><source>J Med Microbiol</source><volume>49</volume><fpage>525</fpage><lpage>534</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10847206</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ehp-116-1352"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diwan</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramljak</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Anver</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gorelick</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ward</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hursting</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Persistent transmission of <italic>Helicobacter hepaticus</italic> via transplacental and/or translactational routes: induction of hepatitis and liver tumors in infected mice [Abstract]</article-title><source>Int J Med Microbiol</source><volume>291</volume><issue>suppl 31</issue><fpage>131</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11437336</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ehp-116-1352"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diwan</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ward</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramljak</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Promotion by <italic>Helicobacter hepaticus</italic>-induced hepatitis of hepatic tumors initiated by <italic>N</italic>-nitrosodimethylamine in male A/JCr mice</article-title><source>Toxicol Pathol</source><volume>25</volume><fpage>597</fpage><lpage>605</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9437805</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ehp-116-1352"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Erdman</surname><given-names>SE</given-nam